WEBVTT

01
00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:14.064
This is Recent styles, a version of Value rows. Each change still means opening a row, so Quick style also keeps the last few whole styles you made.

02
00:00:14.464 --> 00:00:19.277
Select a shape, and each property shows its value in a field you can open.

03
00:00:19.776 --> 00:00:23.970
Style the rectangle one row at a time. First, a green stroke.

04
00:00:26.614 --> 00:00:28.120
Then a light green background.

05
00:00:30.716 --> 00:00:33.621
And the edges go from round to sharp.

06
00:00:35.934 --> 00:00:52.250
Now open Quick style. The style you just made comes first, under Recently used. Below it are the six quick styles, with plain names like Filled, Lines and Crossed lines.

07
00:00:52.756 --> 00:00:58.674
Select the ellipse. Quick style stays open, so the whole style is one click.

08
00:00:58.979 --> 00:01:04.800
The diamond, the same. A style you make once is one click on every next shape.

09
00:01:05.252 --> 00:01:11.871
Everything else is still in the panel. The full palette, with shades and a hex code, opens in place.

10
00:01:15.417 --> 00:01:21.782
So do Stroke width, Fill, Stroke style, Sloppiness and Opacity.

11
00:01:29.783 --> 00:01:33.223
Layers and the actions share one row of icons at the bottom.

12
00:01:35.234 --> 00:01:43.506
What works well: restyling shape after shape takes one click, there's nothing to set up, and each tile shows its style in its own colors.

13
00:01:44.205 --> 00:01:55.139
What's harder: the first shape still takes two clicks per change, the tiles have no names, so two close styles can look alike, and Quick style gets a line taller.
